{
  "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
  "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "MITCHELL P. REICH",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MITCHELL P. REICH, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MICHAEL R. HUSTON",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MICHAEL R. HUSTON, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 18-1269, Rodriguez versus the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question presented in this case is what body of law courts should apply to determine ownership of consolidated tax refunds. In our view, the answer to that question is straightforward. Courts should apply state law. That's the body of law that virtually always governs property rights disputes in our federal system, and, here, the political branches have not displaced that traditional area of state power either by statute or by federal regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the lower courts, the FDIC advocated a rule of federal common law known as the Bob Richards rule, which holds that ownership of a tax refund presumptively resides with the subsidiary whose losses gave rise to that refund. That's the rule the FDIC has advocated for decades, and that's the rule the Tenth Circuit applied below."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Before you proceed with that argument, you now said your question presented was about Bob Richards. You say that the government has abandoned that position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why should we take up Bob Richards at all in this case? Because both sides agree that that's not what should be dispositive, and the Tenth Circuit said here we have a contract, calls for contract interpretation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Excuse me. May I -- because you're going to have to point to something in -- some words in the opinion that do that. I -- I -- I read the opinion. You're right, it said Bob Richards sets out the rule. But the first step of Bob Richards is: Does the contract tell us who has interim ownership? That's how I read the opinion. Does state law trump a contract allocation of ownership?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the contract said you're my agent, as clearly as that, would state law go any further? Would it change that statement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE BREYER",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Was this argued below?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE BREYER",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, it doesn't. It says taking into account Colorado case law. You happened to leave those words out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0000-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it enough then for us to say in your view that the Bob Richards rule is not good law and then to send it back?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Reich",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the government's refusal to defend the Bob Richards rule isn't a reason to not reach the question. I -- I think that it's a sophisticated litigant; it certainly shouldn't be encouraged for declining to answer what's clearly the question presented."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This refund is $4 million."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "when the IRS paid the $4 million tax refund at issue in this case, the bank was entitled to receive that amount within 10 business days."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry, now let's stop. Assume this was that case. Assume this agreement doesn't specify anything, all right? Can the Bob Richards rule stand? And why should it stand?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Can I before -- I just don't want you to stop. I like where you're going. It's interesting and helpful. But I have two related questions. You're assuming throughout that Colorado law does give the money to the bank. Okay. On pages 16 and 17 of their reply brief, they say no, Colorado law does not because Colorado law requires control by -- of the agent Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But what you're talking about, you're talking about general agency law, which is to say you're talking about state law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: -- ask you this way: If the IRS reg leads you to a different answer, as you described it, than state law does, what happens?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think I'll start by what my friends conceded at the podium, which is that on the sole question on which this Court granted certiorari, is the Bob Richards rule valid, the answer is no, that that rule is not a valid rule of federal common law and that courts should not apply it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government's position, which has been consistent for decades, is that an agreement must contain specific language that conclusively disavows the Bob Richards rule in order to depart from this presumption."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you disagree with that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1269",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2d3c9def0f46f4396731888707f6de6f68a64de341e4c3661dce33166ec2e62b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2d3c9def0f46-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
